# Build output. `make build` puts everything here, so ONE entry covers every
# tool that will ever exist — including ones not written yet.
/bin/

# `go build ./cmd/x` from the repo root drops the binary beside the source
# instead. These named entries are a backstop for that.
#
# THE NAMED LIST IS NOT THE DEFENCE. It has now failed three times: /lens was
# missing and a 3.3 MB binary reached a published module zip; /plumb was missing
# and CI caught it on push; then /bin/ itself was dropped while adding /plumb
# and five binaries went into a commit. An allowlist of names fails OPEN — the
# real defence is the "No committed binaries" check in .github/workflows/test.yml.
/ratchet
/strata
/lens
/docket
/plumb

# Coverage output
cover.out
*.out
